  "adaptations": {
    "native": "Real MyGo Checkbox through public control.Checkbox and FieldWith; scopes and Elements exist only within the current build. Native/Flyout menu selection changes configuration selectors; checkboxes keep the same native input and shadcn visual model.",
    "models": "Each recipe owns independent bool fields, selection rows and horizontal scroll state. Source state remains after style/configuration/page changes.",
    "table": "The original source has boolean checked=allSelected, not indeterminate. Partial selections keep the header unchecked. Row1 initially selected in both independent tables; selecting the header updates all four actual row values. Native controls receive explicit nonvisual labels and native table semantics; a bounded native horizontal viewport preserves all original names/emails/roles. Preferred minimum width is600DIP as a native layout adaptation.",
    "widths": "Docs Basic/Disabled/Invalid use224DIP and Description288DIP; Demo/RTL max384DIP. Create unspecified widths and docs no-width group are bounded to384DIP in the native Gallery.",
    "defaults": "Docs Demo/RTL terms2=true; Description=true. Docs desktop group Hard disks/External disks=true while Create Group has all false and no description. Create Title first=true and second disabled; docs whole-card notification starts false.",
    "styling": "The existing fixed Vega source uses FieldGroup gap28 and horizontal rich-control top offset1DIP. Disabled source title cards keep the boundary/description opaque and dim only title/check; fluent overrides preserve native disabled semantics. Plain docs demo/RTL Label uses leading-none; group labels use font-normal.",
    "rtl": "Original English/Arabic/Hebrew values retained, Arabic default; direction is scoped to the source content.",
    "externalEffects": "Changes update only the application-owned model/status. No new fonts, icons, assets, dependencies, OS settings or external data writes."
  },
  "verification": "One public native Tester flow plus injected independent selector backend. Software images do not establish real OS, assistive-technology, IME, display scaling or platform-font parity."
